      "description": "Watch Estrela vs Sporting CP highlights and goals from Primeira Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. On August 8, 2026 , the Primeira Liga action heated up as Estrela da Amadora faced off against Sporting CP . Fans gathered in anticipation of a high-stakes encounter, with both sides looking to make an early-season statement in a match full of tactical intrigue. VAR Dominates a Tense Opening The first half was a narrative of missed opportunities and significant VAR interventions. Sporting CP controlled long stretches of play, but their efforts were thwarted by a disciplined home defense. In the 31st minute, a potential penalty for Sporting was dismissed after a lengthy review, and Estrela themselves had a goal-line situation checked by VAR just before the halftime whistle, leaving the match scoreless at the break. Sporting Take Control After the Interval The deadlock was broken almost immediately after the restart. In the 46th minute, Rodrigo Zalazar found the net with a clinical right-footed finish following an assist from Geny Catamo . Sporting CP appeared to have secured the points in the 59th minute when Fotis Ioannidis tapped home from close range after more fine work from Zalazar , doubling the visitors' lead and silencing the home crowd. Estrela’s Spirited Fightback Despite trailing by two, Estrela da Amadora refused to back down. Leandro Antonetti sparked the revival in the 72nd minute, beating the goalkeeper from distance after a setup by Ianis Stoica . The momentum swung drastically, and in the 84th minute, Beni Souza completed the comeback with a well-placed left-footed shot assisted by Robinho . A chaotic final few minutes saw yellow cards for Beni Souza and Jesse Derry , but neither side could find a winner in what finished as a dramatic 2-2 draw."
